From 9dbb25cfd8605a109045af5795270363689a37de Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <c@local>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 22:09:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Oil pressure: settable time to build pressure and restart
 lock after an oil shutdown

Plan item 57 (from the outra-ecu T20K manual, oil pressure alert).
- oilPressureStartTimeout: time after start for the oil pressure to reach
  'After start minimum oil pressure', or the engine is shut off (0 = 5 s,
  the old fixed value)
- oilRestartLockTime: after the engine was shut off for low oil pressure
  (after-start check, running low oil protection, or an alert on oil
  pressure with the Engine off action) a new start is blocked (no fuel, no
  spark) for this long once the engine has stopped; turning the key off
  ends the lock; 0 = off (default)
- new cut reason 26 "Oil restart lock"
- AlertManager::isEngineOffBy(sensor)
- TunerStudio: Low oil pressure protection dialog
- 6 new tests

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012qcg6EYkigZc99xZ8xdABd
