Subject: [PATCH] Tune selector switch on an analog input, outra-ecu style

Plan item 58 (from the outra-ecu T20K manual, map selector by voltage).
- tuneSelectorChannel: analog input of a tune selector switch; 0-5 V is
  split in equal bands, one per tune (3 tunes: below 1.67 V tune 1, up to
  3.33 V tune 2, above tune 3)
- moving the switch picks its tune, also with the engine running; 0.1 V
  hysteresis at the band edges; empty tunes are skipped as before; the
  tune button and the app still work, the last change wins
- TunerStudio: Tunes dialog
- 5 new tests

